As a healer specialist, I'm going to have to disagree.  As long as you
don't go around burdened, you'll have plenty of time between prayers
so that you don't even need food.  In fact, usually I have enough
actual food to eat that I can use my first 1 or 2 prayers to increase
my max HP above 15.  And you don't need tripe to loot shops...just
make sure you don't let your pet pick up any other objects anywhere
else in the dungeon and it will have plenty of apport to use for
bringing you the piles of gold you drop in the shops.  In my
experience, the worst problem for a healer is losing your pet to a
monster or trap on level 1.

